<title>SOUTH KOREA: S.Korea's Jan-Sept energy demand up 9.7 pct yr/yr.</title>
<headline>S.Korea's Jan-Sept energy demand up 9.7 pct yr/yr.</headline>
<dateline>SEOUL 1996-11-18</dateline>
<text>
<p>South Korea's energy demand rose 9.7 percent to 118.08 million tonnes of oil equivalent (TOE) in the first nine months of 1996 from 107.67 million a year-ago period, the Ministry of Trade, Industry and Energy said on Monday.</p>
<p>Rising use of liquefied natural gas (LNG) for home fuel and hydroelectric power generation was behind the growth, a ministry statement said.</p>
<p>However, oil products consumption growth slowed due to an industrial slowdown, it said.  </p>
<p>Breakdown of South Korea's energy demand in the nine-month period, compared with the same 1995 period. (Figures in brackets are year-on-year growth in percentage):</p>
<p>				Jan-Sept 1996	 Jan-Sept 1995</p>
<p>				Amount		  Amount</p>
<p> Total		     118,080   (9.7)     107,669   (9.4)</p>
<p>(in 1,000 TOE)</p>
<p> Petroleum products    517,474   (7.2)     482,863   (9.2)</p>
<p>(in 1,000 barrels)</p>
<p> LNG (in 1,000 tonnes)   6,416  (32.4)	 4,845  (21.3)</p>
<p> Hard coal		   3,105 (-15.6)	 3,680 (-20.9)</p>
<p>(in 1,000 tonnes)</p>
<p> Bituminous coal	  31,552  (12.5)	28,043   (8.2)</p>
<p>(in 1,000 tonnes)</p>
<p> Nuclear power	    55,794  (12.4)	49,626  (12.0)</p>
<p>(in gigawatt hours)</p>
<p> Hydroelectric power     4,143  (-2.2)	 4,235  (28.2)</p>
<p>(in gigawatt hours)</p>
<p> Others			  831  (10.8)	   749  (16.1)</p>
<p>(in 1,000 TOE)</p>
<p>Source: Ministry of Trade, Industry and Energy</p>
<p>--Seoul Newsroom (822) 727 5643</p>
